  "_riyadhVenueSourceSecondPass": "2026-09-15, at explicit user request ('i need more venues than just 17'): a second research pass per district, this time explicitly pushing Arabic-language sourcing (the first pass searched mostly in English; Riyadh's real independent scene is much better documented in Arabic, confirmed repeatedly this round) and telling each agent exactly what the first pass already found so nothing duplicated. Landed 9 more genuine, verified venues: Olaya +2 (Hewar Art Gallery, Lyrs Artisan Bakery), Diriyah +3 (HODAJ, Ghaymat Samhan, Saba Lounge), JAX District +3 (OffBrief, With Heart, Personage), Hittin +1 (Kasbah) — bringing the Riyadh total to 26 across the 5 districts. Several of these have a thinner verification trail than this file's usual bar (no named owner, verification resting on 'no evidence of a second site' rather than a positive ownership record) — flagged here rather than silently treated as equivalent to a fully-sourced entry, since Riyadh's smaller independents generally have much less English or even Arabic web presence than this file's UK venues did at the same stage. Woods Specialty Café (Olaya, at the 3-site cap and actively soliciting franchise partners on franchisecenter.sa) and Sharq (Diriyah, a 3-city restaurant with no identifiable small owner, reading as an organically-expanding chain rather than a sibling-pair) were both found and dropped for real chain-signal reasons; Avak (Hittin) and Petit Café (Hittin) were dropped on the same 'when unsure, drop' basis the whole project has held to — Avak's possible link to Aline Kamakian's multi-city Mayrig group couldn't be ruled out, and Petit Café's identical name to an established Beirut original (trademark-marked) plus a London outpost reads as an imported concept, not a single Riyadh operator. KAFD stayed at 2 venues despite a dedicated second pass: the only new leads found (Sira, Cloud 14, Riya Maison, Lafana, Kanza Pool Lounge) are all brand-new restaurants inside Atheel and W Riyadh, two hotels that had literally opened about a week before this research ran — real candidates for a future pass once they have actual independent verification (reviews, confirmed walk-in/public access) rather than just opening-announcement coverage, not included here since that would be publishing an unconfirmed lead as settled data. Introduces 2 new venue types: TEA HOUSE (HODAJ) is now wired to the real 'Tea houses' Riyadh Drink tile in src/lib/scoring/tile-catalog-map.ts, closing one of the three gaps the first pass left open; MOROCCAN LOUNGE (Kasbah) is left category-only (Drink) — distinct enough from every existing Drink type (not hotel-based, not a shisha-only concept) to warrant its own label. 'Mocktail lounges' and 'Juice & smoothie bars' still match zero venues — the two remaining real gaps for whenever the next Riyadh pass happens.",
  "_dailyReviewPromotionSource20260915": "2026-09-15: curia-suggestion-review's daily pass independently re-verified and promoted all 10 candidates sitting in docs/data/venue-suggestions.json as 'pending' with a 2026-09-15 suggestedDate (Cinemac and Amazing India, Macclesfield; Bar Six and Drift Art Gallery, Nantwich; Prestbury Cricket Club; Sticky Fingers Bakery, Stockport (Underbanks); 78 Degrees, Bramhall; T.La Art & Craft Gallery, Chinatown; Heaton Moor Park and Beer Shop, Heaton Moor) via two parallel fresh independent web-research passes, coordinates re-checked/tightened against real postcode centroids (all within ~40m of the original candidates' figures except Drift Art Gallery, which stays an acknowledged approximation on Nantwich High Street per the original candidate's own flag), reason copy checked against Brand voice and left unchanged (all ten already read cleanly, none asserted a site-count claim that needed correcting in user-facing copy). Duplicate-checked against both the live venues array (190 entries) and every other suggestions-file entry regardless of status — no collisions. All 10 default to petFriendly:false/dietaryOptions:['none'] on a genuine no-signal-found basis (today's re-verification focused on chain-status/trading-status, not diet/pet specifics) — same conservative-default rule as every prior pass, to be revisited by a future pass the way most of the existing 190 already have been. Two candidates needed real judgment calls rather than a clean pass: Bar Six's 'single site' framing turned out to be wrong — it's actually a real 3-site family group (Stephen and Jack Mitchell: Bar Six Sandbach 2017, Six Nantwich 2021, Six Knutsford Sept 2024), all Cheshire-only, opened roughly one every 3-7 years with no stated further-expansion plans; judged within the same small-sibling-group allowance already established by Wallop's own 3-site Knutsford/Prestwich/Didsbury precedent and The Creameries' 3-site Pomona Island Brew Co. precedent elsewhere in this file, not a chain — promoted as-is since the site-count error was never reflected in the user-facing reason copy anyway. T.La Art & Craft Gallery's single Companies House registration (T.LA ARTS AND CRAFT GALLERY LIMITED, since 2002, same Nicholas Street address) was confirmed, but a Facebook page suggesting a possible second 'Wing Yip Centre branch' couldn't be conclusively resolved either way (Facebook itself was unreachable to this session); promoted anyway since even a genuine 2-site outcome would still clear the same allowance, so the ambiguity doesn't change the verdict. One unconfirmed rumor was weighed and dismissed rather than acted on: a single AI-search-summary result claimed a March 2026 'foreclosure notice' at Amazing India's unit, naming a company (Selmar Properties Ltd) with no findable tie to Macclesfield or this address anywhere in company records or local press, contradicted by an Active Companies House status and Tripadvisor reviews into August 2025 — judged not credible enough to withhold promotion, flagged here so a future closure-audit pass knows to give Amazing India a second look rather than rediscovering this from scratch. A minor internal-notes-only correction (not reflected in any promoted copy): Amazing India's owner is Joby Joy with business partner Prema Pillai, not the married 'Joby and Prema Pillai' framing the original candidate implied. Zero rejections this run. The remaining three pending-review-queue.json items (Prana/Altrincham, Buon Cibo/Heaton Moor, Rustik/Didsbury) were checked against Curia Command's pending_review collection (empty, no decision recorded) and left unchanged — no new evidence surfaced for any of them this run. The day's closure-audit rotating slice (indices 150-154: Prestbury Golf Club, The Beer House, The Garden Eatery, The Edge, Bramall Hall) found no closures — all five re-confirmed still trading (Bramall Hall is mid an ~18-month roof-restoration project with some areas phased-closed, but the Hall itself remains open to visitors, not a closure signal).",
  "_chicagoVenueSource": "36 real venues added 2026-09-18 for Curia's first US metro (Hyde Park/Kenwood/Woodlawn, Chicago), at explicit user request — a pilot for a specific first member (a UChicago student, high disposable income, testing/showing the app to professors), scoped to roughly 2mi of the UChicago campus rather than the whole city. Researched via three independent, parallel research passes (one per neighbourhood), each individually address-verified against the real community-area boundary (not loose 'near Kenwood'-style tags, which turned out to be unreliable — a meaningful number of initially-promising Kenwood/Woodlawn leads were rejected as actually being in Hyde Park, Bronzeville, or permanently closed). 26 Hyde Park, 3 Kenwood (genuinely thin — a real, quiet, historic mansion district with little commercial footprint, same honest-yield precedent as Mobberley/Hittin/KAFD elsewhere in the app), 7 Woodlawn (2 genuinely seasonal — 7323 Chicago Café and 61st Street Farmers Market are both closed Nov–April, noted in their own descriptions since the data model has no seasonal-flag field yet). Every address geocoded via Nominatim/OpenStreetMap (free, no key) — the US-address equivalent of the postcodes.io method already used for UK venues. Real per-venue distinctiveness/ownership reasoning (Hard rule 1's two-gate model) lives in supabase/migrations/0021_chicago_hyde_park_kenwood_woodlawn.sql, not in this JSON (same split as the Cheshire golf clubs pass — see _cheshireGolfClubsSource). One real ownership judgment call worth restating here: Tafari's Kitchen (Obama Presidential Center) is chef-curated by a small South-Side-only restaurant group but day-to-day operated under contract by Bon Appétit/Compass Group, a large national caterer — scored as small_group on the strength of the chef-driven, site-unique concept, with the operational nuance kept visible in ownership_notes rather than resolved silently either way. Alcohol is legal and normal here (unlike Riyadh), so Chicago stays fully 'uk' HomeRegion — the existing shared global Drink catalog, not a new region split; the member's age doesn't change what gets curated. 10 new venue types introduced (CAFETERIA, DIVE BAR, RECORD SHOP, CARIBBEAN RESTAURANT, SOUTHERN RESTAURANT, INDIAN-SOUTHERN FUSION, CREOLE-BRAZILIAN, SENEGALESE, DINER, SOUL FOOD) — 5 wired into the existing 'Neighbourhood favourite' tile (cafeteria, caribbean-restaurant, senegalese, diner, soul-food, all honest-fixture-register fits), the rest left category-only, same convention as every other US/non-UK cuisine type in this catalog.",
  "_chicagoCampusVenueSource": "10 real UChicago campus venues added 2026-09-18, at explicit user request — a personal customization of the Chicago metro specifically for the brother it was built for (a real UChicago student): 'lots of libraries and bookstores as well as college campus venues like the food hall and the library and the gym'. Deliberately scoped to touch nothing outside Chicago and nothing in the global onboarding tile catalog — these 4 new venue types (ACADEMIC LIBRARY, PUBLIC LIBRARY, CAMPUS DINING HALL, CAMPUS GYM) are category-only in tile-catalog-map.ts (CATEGORY_BY_VENUE_TYPE), never added to docs/data/tiles.json or TILE_NAME_TO_VENUE_TYPE_SLUGS — no new onboarding tile appears for any member anywhere, including him; the venues are simply richly present when actually browsing Hyde Park/Kenwood/Woodlawn on Map/List or under the mood filter's Do/Eat category matching. 2 academic libraries (Joseph Regenstein + the adjoining Mansueto, treated as one entry since they share one entrance/access policy; John Crerar, the university's separate science/medicine library), 2 public libraries (Blackstone Branch — the first CPL branch ever purpose-built, privately funded, fills out Kenwood's own flagged-thin coverage; Bessie Coleman Branch, Woodlawn), 4 real current dining commons (Baker, Bartlett, Cathey, and International House's — the historic Bartlett/Baker/Cathey set plus a fourth, newer one easy to miss), 2 athletics facilities (Ratner, Henry Crown Field House). One real, honestly-flagged Gate 1 nuance: the libraries and dining halls are genuinely walk-in accessible to anyone (free library passes; dining halls take a card at the door, no meal plan required — verified, not assumed) and pass Gate 1 cleanly, but the two CAMPUS GYM venues require membership or a student-sponsored guest pass — not open-door walk-in — flagged plainly in each one's own ownership_notes rather than silently treated as equivalent to everything else in the catalog. Ownership is 'independent' across all ten as the honest fit for a single, non-replicated public/academic institution — a genuine stretch of a field designed for commercial chain-detection, noted here rather than pretending it's a clean fit. Two real venues were researched and deliberately excluded: O'Gara & Wilson Booksellers (the historic Hyde Park antiquarian shop) has relocated out of Chicago entirely, now in Chesterton, IN; Ex Libris Theological Books is closed. A new Barnes & Noble opened in the Hyde Park Shopping Center in 2026 — real and current, excluded on Hard Rule 1 Gate 1 grounds (a national chain) regardless of freshness. Distinctiveness/ownership values are in supabase/migrations/0023_chicago_campus_venues.sql, not this JSON — same split as every other pass tonight.",
  "_padelTennisVenueSource": "11 real standalone padel/tennis venues added 2026-09-18, at explicit user follow-up on the Play sport tile ('we should keep padel and tennis but we should source some venues'). Researched via four parallel passes (existing golf clubs checked for padel/tennis facilities; standalone padel clubs; standalone tennis clubs, both Manchester/Cheshire). 4 padel (The Pollen Club and Club de Padel in central Manchester; Adlington Padel, a family golf centre outside Macclesfield; Manchester Padel Club, Heald Green), 7 tennis — deliberately excluding 4 real, verified clubs (Didsbury LTC, Nantwich TC, Chester LTC, Lindow LTC) that the research pass itself flagged as not clearing Curia's real Gate 2 bar (competent but nothing distinctive found), same 'don't pad with weak entries' discipline as every other pass tonight. The Northern Lawn Tennis Club is a genuine find: Sampras won his first grass-court title there, Connors and McEnroe both played it, real Davis Cup history. Four existing golf clubs also had real padel/tennis facilities found and tagged directly (sub_preference_tags), not added as new venues: Dunham Forest (2 padel courts), Fairmont Cheshire/The Mere (padel, via Surge Padel), Champneys Mottram Hall (3 padel courts, 'The Hook Club') all gained Padel; Carden Park (2 dual tennis courts) gained Tennis. Nine other golf clubs were checked and confirmed to have neither (Wilmslow, Prestbury, Delamere Forest, Sandiway, Vale Royal Abbey, Wychwood Park, Macdonald Portal, Warrington, Chester, Alderley Edge, Congleton, Malkins Bank, Crewe, Helsby, Knutsford, Lymm, Macclesfield golf clubs — full list in the research). New venue types PADEL CLUB and TENNIS CLUB wired into the existing 'Play sport' tile (tile-catalog-map.ts), Golf/Padel/Tennis all now genuinely backed by real venues for the first time. Real per-venue distinctiveness/ownership reasoning in supabase/migrations/0024_padel_tennis_venues.sql, not this JSON — same split as every other research pass tonight.",
  "_ciboMuckyPupCoordinateFixSource": "2026-09-18, at direct user report: Cibo and The Mucky Pup were rendering identically stacked on the map, one hiding the other. Root cause found on inspection: both venues shared the exact coordinate 53.326377,-2.230888 — which turned out to be the SK9 1LD postcode's own centroid (confirmed via postcodes.io), not either venue's real building. Whoever originally geocoded these two evidently fell back to a shared postcode-level point for at least one of them, rather than the real per-address geocoding this file's other entries use (see curia_venue_coordinate_methodology). Re-geocoded both from their real street addresses via Nominatim: Cibo, 26-28 Green Lane (SK9 1LD) -> 53.326515,-2.230945; The Mucky Pup, 15 Grove Street (SK9 1DU, a genuinely different postcode from Cibo's, despite an initial WebSearch snippet wrongly suggesting they shared one) -> 53.327081,-2.231014, the latter a direct named-POI match in OpenStreetMap itself ('The Mucky Pup, 13-15, Grove Street'), not just an address-text geocode. The two real buildings are about 65m apart on parallel streets — genuinely close neighbours, but no longer literally on top of each other. Applied directly via SQL (supabase/migrations/0030_cibo_mucky_pup_coordinates.sql).",
  "_chicagoPlaySportVenuesSource": "2026-09-18, at explicit user follow-up after being asked directly whether the 'Play sport' tile (golf/padel/tennis) actually has any real matches in Chicago — it didn't: all 33 golf/padel/tennis venues in the dataset were Manchester/Cheshire-only, a real, honest gap for the specific member Chicago was built for. Researched real venues within Chicago's own established ~2mi campus scope (see MetroId's own doc comment in src/types/models.ts — 'not the whole city'), not the wider metro. Jackson Park Golf Course (6401 S Richards Dr, geocoded via Nominatim, 1.5mi from campus, in Woodlawn) is real and verified — Chicago Park District's oldest public course, opened 1899 inside Frederick Law Olmsted and Daniel Burnham's Jackson Park (built for the 1893 World's Columbian Exposition), the first public golf course anywhere west of the Allegheny Mountains, its historic clubhouse renamed for Cecil A. Partee in 1997; pay-and-play, no membership needed, the cleanest Gate 1 pass of any golf venue added this session. Hyde Park Tennis Club (1301 E 47th St, 1.3mi from campus, in Kenwood) is real and verified — a private club running continuously since 1913 (109 members by its first full year), five lit courts, no court-booking system, members simply turn up; flagged honestly as membership-required, same disclosure precedent as the CAMPUS GYM venues in migration 0023, not smoothed over. Padel deliberately NOT added: the nearest real padel clubs (Cube Padel Chicago, Back of the Yards, ~4mi; Union Padel Club, West Loop, ~7.4mi) are both well outside Chicago's established campus-scoped radius — padding the tile with a venue nobody in Hyde Park would actually walk to would be worse than leaving the gap honest, same standard the original UK padel/tennis pass (_padelTennisVenueSource) set of not inventing venues to look fuller. Distinctiveness/ownership applied directly via SQL (supabase/migrations/0027_chicago_golf_tennis_venues.sql), same convention as every other Chicago venue — not stored as JSON fields here, see that migration's own reasoning.",
